{"Title":"An Act authorizing Matthew K. Sonnabend to purchase creditable service from the Barnstable County Retirement Board","BillNumber":"S2526","DocketNumber":null,"GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"S29","Name":"Senate Committee on Rules","Type":2,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/S29","ResponseDate":"2023-12-15T11:25:26.63"},"Cosponsors":[],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S2526/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Amendment","Pinslip":"Senate, December 18, 2023 -- The committee on Senate Rules, to whom was referred the House Bill authorizing Matthew K. Sonnabend to purchase creditable service from the Barnstable County Retirement Board (House, No. 3643),- reports, recommending that the matter be placed in the Orders of the Day for the next session with an amendment striking out all after the enacting clause and inserting in place thereof the text contained in Senate document numbered 2526.","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1. Notwithstanding section 3 of chapter 71 of the acts of 1996 or any other general or special law to the contrary, the Barnstable county retirement board shall permit Matthew K. Sonnabend, a member of the Barnstable county retirement system, to purchase creditable service for his military service time pursuant to paragraph (h) of subdivision (1) of section 4 of chapter 32 of the General Laws regardless of whether he is a member in service or a retiree at the time of said purchase.\r\n\tSECTION 2. This act shall take effect upon its passage.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[],"Amendments":[]}